TEMPORARY vendor patch — maintainer ruling record 6845302116 (objectstack
card "SCIM: a PATCH that replaces only name.givenName / name.familyName leaves
displayName and sys_user.name on the old name", option C). The ruling sets
AGENTS.md's "No workarounds ... not temporary patches" aside for this patch
only; patches/ gains no other better-auth patch.

What it changes: setNamePart() stored the part and never recomposed
name.formatted / displayName (composeName() served only the name.formatted
remove path). It now recomposes name.formatted, and through setFormattedName()
displayName, when name.formatted equalled composeName() of the parts BEFORE
the part changed. An explicit (non-derived) name is never overwritten.

Removal condition: delete this file and its patchedDependencies row in the
upgrade PR to the first @better-auth/scim release that ships the recompose.
The regression pin packages/plugins/plugin-auth/src/scim-name-recompose.test.ts
stays.

